WEBVTT

00:00:15.767 --> 00:00:17.254
<v><b>Greg:</b></v> Hi! I’m Greg.

00:00:17.607 --> 00:00:18.847
Welcome to Oxford.

00:00:19.667 --> 00:00:22.344
I’m visiting the Old Bank Hotel.

00:00:23.250 --> 00:00:26.500
It’s an unusual hotel in the centre of the city.

00:00:27.547 --> 00:00:31.105
The Old Bank is in the High Street, in the centre of Oxford.

00:00:31.558 --> 00:00:35.568
Today it’s a luxury hotel, but these buildings –

00:00:35.610 --> 00:00:38.288
from number ninety-two to number ninety-four –

00:00:38.634 --> 00:00:41.162
have a very interesting history.

00:00:42.782 --> 00:00:47.020
In the sixteenth century, they were part of Christ Church College.

00:00:48.407 --> 00:00:51.880
In the eighteenth century, they were different shops.

00:00:54.356 --> 00:00:59.006
And we know that in 1808 the buildings were one business –

00:01:01.745 --> 00:01:02.520
a bank.

00:01:05.152 --> 00:01:08.064
There was a bank here for almost two hundred years,

00:01:08.480 --> 00:01:11.457
but today it’s a famous Oxford hotel.

00:01:12.357 --> 00:01:13.730
Would you like to go in and look?

00:01:14.730 --> 00:01:15.320
Let’s go.

00:01:23.311 --> 00:01:26.701
The Old Bank Hotel has a beautiful reception

00:01:27.468 --> 00:01:29.321
and a fantastic restaurant.

00:01:32.315 --> 00:01:34.066
There are forty-two bedrooms

00:01:34.572 --> 00:01:36.447
and they’re all very comfortable.

00:01:38.600 --> 00:01:41.917
They have great views of Oxford’s famous colleges.

00:01:44.659 --> 00:01:53.188
This room has a large bed, two chairs, a table, a television, and a cupboard.

00:01:54.948 --> 00:01:57.467
It has a beautiful marble bathroom, too.

00:02:01.009 --> 00:02:05.793
But there are other rooms that visitors to the hotel don’t usually see.

00:02:06.647 --> 00:02:12.556
These secret rooms are here in the cellar, under the hotel.

00:02:14.496 --> 00:02:17.071
These are the old bank vaults.

00:02:17.590 --> 00:02:21.093
When the hotel was a bank, all the money was here.

00:02:22.527 --> 00:02:26.119
The rooms were small and the doors weren’t easy to open!

00:02:27.032 --> 00:02:29.551
They were very, very strong,

00:02:30.217 --> 00:02:33.031
and on each one, there was a large lock.

00:02:35.025 --> 00:02:38.586
Today, these old vaults are storerooms.

00:02:40.966 --> 00:02:45.880
The hotel keeps its wine collection in here, so it’s very, very safe!

00:02:48.319 --> 00:02:52.475
Ninety-two to ninety-four High Street is a part of Oxford’s history.

00:02:52.935 --> 00:02:58.531
And today, if you want to visit Oxford, the Old Bank is a fantastic place to see!